(a) Oversight and non-compliance. The chief procurement officer of central services, along with CCD staff and staff for each county user department, shall report any potential occurrence(s) of non-compliance with these program requirements by prime contractors and subcontractors during the term of the contract. The CCD shall recommend appropriate mechanisms to enforce the provisions of this program to the contract administrator. The failure of a bidder or participant to comply with the requirements of this chapter may be grounds for penalties, including possible suspension or debarment, by the contracts administrator pursuant to the standards set forth in this chapter.
(b) Other violations. It shall also be a violation of this program to:
(1) Fraudulently obtain, retain, or attempt to obtain/retain (or aid another in fraudulently obtaining, retaining, or attempting to obtain/retain) certification status as an SLBE for purposes of this program;
(2) Willfully falsify, conceal, or cover up by a trick, scheme, or device, a material fact pertaining to the provisions of this program;
(3) Knowingly make any false, fictitious, or fraudulent statements or representations, or make use of any false writing or document, knowing the same to contain any false, fictitious, or fraudulent statement or representation pertaining to the provisions of this program;
(4) Willfully obstruct, impede, or attempt to obstruct/impede any authorized official or employee who is investigating the qualifications of a business entity which has requested certification as an SLBE;
(5) Fraudulently obtain, attempt to obtain (or aid another person fraudulently obtaining or attempting to obtain) public monies to which the person is not entitled under the provisions of this program; or
(6) Make a false statement to any business entity or government representative that another entity is or is not certified as an SLBE for purposes of this program.
Any person who violates the provisions of this section shall be subject to the penalties and sanctions set forth below in section 2-151.3 as well as any other remedies available under law up to the maximum penalty provided by law.
(Ord. No. 2024-153, § 1, 6-4-24; Ord. No. 2024-169, § 1, 7-2-24)

